<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Le Dai Hanh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">941–1005</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Lê Đại Hành, Le Hoan, Lê Hoàn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Le Dai Hanh, born Le Hoan, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-le-dynasty">Early Le dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, ruling from 980 to 1005. A commander under the Dinh dynasty, he took the throne with the backing of the queen mother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duong-van-nga">Duong Van Nga</a>. In 981 he defeated a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> invasion, and in 982 he campaigned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a> and sacked its capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/le-dai-hanh.jpg" alt="Le Dai Hanh" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kien1980v at Vietnamese Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ledaihanh.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
